Description: Wild OS pop-ups: screenshots, clipboard history and emoji
 The overlays Windows people reach for by shortcut:
 .
  * Win+Shift+S and Print Screen: the Wild OS screenshot toolbar, with
    rectangle, window, full screen and freehand captures, screen
    recording and a delay. Captures go to the clipboard and to
    Pictures/Screenshots, with a toast to mark them up or share them.
  * Win+V and Win+full stop: one panel for clipboard history (Klipper's,
    with pins that survive a restart), emoji and symbols, pasted straight
    into the app you were using.
  * The QML pieces the shell uses for its toasts and on-screen displays:
    placing a window on a screen edge above everything, and Caps Lock and
    Num Lock state.
 .
 The clipboard history uses the private QML module of Plasma's clipboard
 widget, so it is tied to the Plasma version named in the dependencies.
